80	Parallel and Distributed Computing — Calculus Edition	1	Speedup	exact_linear	control,parallel	A ratio of two execution times.	Linear speedup 𝑆𝑝= 𝑝is the ideal, and superlinear speedup indicates a cache effect — the aggregate cache grew with the processor count, so the comparison baseline changed. It is a ratio, so it does not compose additively.	Speedup is a time ratio; superlinearity signals a changed baseline.	Exact linear.
